Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Custom Back Button + Navigation Interception

```csharp
// EditProductPage.xaml.cs
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();

        // Custom "Cancel" back button
        Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
        {
            TextOverride = "Cancel",
            Command = new Command(async () => await TryNavigateBack())
        });
    }

    // Intercept hardware/gesture back navigation
    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the async dialog; return true to cancel navigation
            MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () => await TryNavigateBack());
            return true; // cancel default back
        }
        return false; // allow normal back
    }

    private async Task TryNavigateBack()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave)
                return; // user chose to stay
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }

    // Call this whenever form data changes
    private void OnFormFieldChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
        _hasUnsavedChanges = true;
    }
}
```

## 2. XAML (relevant Shell bits)

```xml
<!-- EditProductPage.xaml -->
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Title="Edit Product">

    <!-- BackButtonBehavior is set in code-behind, but can also go here: -->
    <!--
    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                           Command="{Binding BackCommand}" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
    -->

    <VerticalStackLayout Padding="16">
        <Entry Placeholder="Product Name"
               TextChanged="OnFormFieldChanged" />
        <!-- ... other fields ... -->
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
```

## Key points

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Custom back button text | `BackButtonBehavior.TextOverride` |
| Intercept software back | `BackButtonBehavior.Command` |
| Intercept Android HW back / swipe | Override `OnBackButtonPressed()` → return `true` to cancel |
| Navigate back programmatically | `Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..")` |

> **Note:** On iOS, swipe-back gesture isn't caught by `OnBackButtonPressed`. If you need to block that too, set `Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior` with `IsVisible = true` (which disables the swipe gesture when a custom command is set) or disable the gesture via a platform-specific handler.
